{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1743","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"D. Problem with Random Tests"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"4 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"512 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a string $$$s$$$ consisting of $$$n$$$ characters. Each character of $$$s$$$ is either "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A substring of $$$s$$$ is a contiguous subsequence of its characters."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You have to choose two substrings of $$$s$$$ (possibly intersecting, possibly the same, possibly non-intersecting — just any two substrings). After choosing them, you calculate the value of the chosen pair of substrings as follows:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" let $$$s_1$$$ be the first substring, $$$s_2$$$ be the second chosen substring, and $$$f(s_i)$$$ be the integer such that $$$s_i$$$ is its binary representation (for example, if $$$s_i$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11010"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":", $$$f(s_i) = 26$$$); "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" the value is the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"bitwise OR"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" of $$$f(s_1)$$$ and $$$f(s_2)$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Calculate the maximum possible value you can get, and print it "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"in binary representation without leading zeroes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line contains one integer $$$n$$$ — the number of characters in $$$s$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line contains $$$s$$$ itself, consisting of exactly $$$n$$$ characters "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and/or "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"All non-example tests in this problem are generated randomly: every character of $$$s$$$ is chosen independently of other characters; for each character, the probability of it being "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" is exactly $$$\\frac{1}{2}$$$"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"This problem has exactly $$$40$$$ tests. Tests from $$$1$$$ to $$$3$$$ are the examples; tests from $$$4$$$ to $$$40$$$ are generated randomly. In tests from $$$4$$$ to $$$10$$$, $$$n = 5$$$; in tests from $$$11$$$ to $$$20$$$, $$$n = 1000$$$; in tests from $$$21$$$ to $$$40$$$, $$$n = 10^6$$$. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Hacks are forbidden in this problem."}],"kind":"container"}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print the maximum possible value you can get "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"in binary representation without leading zeroes"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n11010\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n11111\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n1110010\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n1111110\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n4\n0000\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first example, you can choose the substrings "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11010"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"101"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". $$$f(s_1) = 26$$$, $$$f(s_2) = 5$$$, their bitwise OR is $$$31$$$, and the binary representation of $$$31$$$ is "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11111"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second example, you can choose the substrings "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"1110010"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" and "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"11100"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"D","problemCode":"1743D","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1743/problem/D"}